## Durable rate-limit recovery follow-up (2026-10-26 21:47 UTC)

- Source now serializes Ollama Search calls by 15 seconds and strict-SO calls
  by 5 seconds. It captures `Retry-After`, `X-RateLimit-Reset`, and bounded
  provider error text; persists the resulting cooldown; pauses the shared
  worker across restarts; and caps long Node timers before re-reading persisted
  cooldown state. Exact no-credentials errors defer for 15 minutes without
  consuming an attempt. Existing five-attempt limit remains for real provider
  failures.
- Search failures stop before strict-SO. Collected source evidence remains
  review-required and unrated, including when score recomputation fails. A
  strict-SO retry stays on the original exact-free connection; if it is no
  longer active and eligible, retry blocks without dispatching on another
  connection and refunds the queue attempt.
- Code Simplifier reviewed the final source/test diff. No further source
  simplification preserved the explicit retry-state and fail-closed branches
  more clearly. Prettier formatted the two modified test files and TODO.
- Verification after the pinning change: targeted benchmark-search tests pass
  9/9, including 429 deferral, repeated 429 limit, no-credentials deferral,
  durable pause, retry parser, bounded timer, and pinned-connection retry;
  search-proxy tests pass 10/10, including header propagation and pacing before
  provider timeout. Migration numbering passes with 196 files, three known
  gaps, and no duplicates; `git diff --check` passes. The full benchmark-search
  file was interrupted after 41 passing cases because one long-running test
  remained in flight; it produced no assertion failures before interruption,
  so full-file completion is unverified.
- `npm run check:docs-all` passes with the Linux esbuild binary selected. The
